DRAFT — written by inspecting fcitx/fcitx5-hangul @ tag 5.1.11
(commit ede437b, matching installed fcitx5-hangul 5.1.11-1), NOT YET
BUILT OR TESTED. See docs/RESEARCH.md "Known limitation" and
docs/NEXT-STEPS.md before using this.

fcitx5-hangul hardcodes its selectable keyboards as a fixed enum
(src/engine.h) plus a parallel id array (src/engine.cpp) — it does not
enumerate whatever libhangul reports. Adding "2sunarae" to libhangul
is therefore necessary but not sufficient; fcitx5-hangul itself needs
these two changes, appending (not inserting, to avoid renumbering
anyone's saved config) a new entry at the end of both lists:

--- a/src/engine.h
+++ b/src/engine.h
@@ enum class HangulKeyboard {
     Romaja,
     Ahnmatae,
+    Dubeolsik_Sunarae,
 };

@@ FCITX_CONFIG_ENUM_NAME_WITH_I18N(HangulKeyboard, N_("Dubeolsik"), ...
-                                 N_("Ahnmatae"));
+                                 N_("Ahnmatae"), N_("Dubeolsik Sun-arae"));

--- a/src/engine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine.cpp
@@ static const char *keyboardId[] = {"2",  "2y", "39", "3f", "3s",
-                                   "3y", "32", "ro", "ahn"};
+                                   "3y", "32", "ro", "ahn", "2sunarae"};

After that, `Keyboard=Dubeolsik Sun-arae` in
~/.config/fcitx5/conf/hangul.conf (see fcitx5/hangul.conf) would select
it through the normal fcitx5-hangul config path — no further code
changes needed since it's still a `2sunarae`-style ("2"-key-table)
keyboard from libhangul's point of view.

Build would follow fcitx5-hangul's normal CMake process:
  cmake -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build
  sudo cmake --install build
(needs `cmake` and `extra-cmake-modules`, not currently installed in
this environment — see docs/NEXT-STEPS.md.)
